INT. FISH PROCESSING PLANT - OFFICE - NIGHT

A glassed-in office above the processing floor. Below, conveyor belts, hoses, steel tables slick with scales. The office smells of brine and cigarettes. A desk lamp. A ledger.

DETECTIVE RAFFERTY (40s, gray overcoat, a face like a closed door) sits across from TULLY (50s, plant owner, rubber apron over a silk shirt, gold chain, hands thick as hams). On the wall, a mounted marlin with a dust-covered eye. Between them: a plastic bag holding a small silver watch.

RAFFERTY
You recognize it?

TULLY
Never seen it.

RAFFERTY
It's engraved. "To D, with love, M."

TULLY
Lots of D's in the world.

RAFFERTY
Lots of M's.

HALVORSEN (30s, plant foreman, hairnet, boots, scales on his forearms) leans on the doorframe, arms crossed. He doesn't enter.

HALVORSEN
Boss, you want me to stay?

TULLY
Go back to the floor.

HALVORSEN
Yes, sir.

He doesn't move. Rafferty notices.

RAFFERTY
Mr. Halvorsen. Stay. I have a question for you.

HALVORSEN
(to Tully)
Boss?

TULLY
(tight)
Answer him.

RAFFERTY
The night shift on the eleventh. You were on?

HALVORSEN
I'm always on.

RAFFERTY
And you saw nothing unusual.

HALVORSEN
Fish.

RAFFERTY
Fish.

He turns to Tully, still polite.

RAFFERTY (CONT'D)
Mr. Tully, I'll be straight with you. I've got a body in the harbor. Male. Late thirties. No wallet, no ring. This was in his hand.

TULLY
Terrible.

RAFFERTY
He had your cigarette brand in his teeth. He had fish scales under his nails. He had a chemical burn on his wrist that I'd say comes from a brine pump.

TULLY
You're making it fit.

RAFFERTY
I'm just listing it.

From below, a hiss of steam and a sudden clang. Tully stiffens. Halvorsen glances at the window. A WOMAN (50s, in a trench coat and rain hat, a briefcase in her hand) is walking across the floor toward the stairs.

TULLY
Who the hell is that?

HALVORSEN
No idea.

The Woman climbs. The office door opens without a knock. She sets her briefcase on the desk, opens it, and takes out a badge: AGENT CORVO, FEDERAL BUREAU.

CORVO
Mr. Tully. I'd like to talk about the shipment of eleven tons of cocaine hidden in your tuna.

Tully stands slowly. Rafferty doesn't. He picks up the watch bag, studies the engraving, and slides it across the desk to Corvo.

RAFFERTY
Agent. He's all yours.

TULLY
(hoarse)
You told me she was a cop.

RAFFERTY
I did.

TULLY
You said she was local.

RAFFERTY
She is. She just works for a bigger office.

Tully turns to the foreman. Halvorsen backs out of the doorway and takes the stairs two at a time. Down on the floor, the belts keep running.
